<title>USA: Cardiovascular Diagnostics sues Boehringer.</title>
<headline>Cardiovascular Diagnostics sues Boehringer.</headline>
<dateline>RALEIGH, N.C. 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cardiovascular Diagnostics Inc said today that it has filed suit againt an American unit of Boehringer Mannheim Gmbh in U.S. District Court, charging it with misappropriation of its trade secrets by improper disclosure, breach of contract, breach of fiduciary duty, unfair and deceptive trade practices and constructive fraud.</p>
<p>The company alleged that Boehringer had entered into an exclusive licensing agreement with it for certain blood coagulation diagnostic assays, but later filed patent applications that contained confidential information, disclosing to the market its trade secrets.</p>
<p>Cardiovascular said it is asking the court for substantial actual and punitive damages.</p>
<p>Boehringer could not be immediately reached for comment.</p>
</text>
